# ORCLFIRE: bullets by source, and what a star does (M16.5).
#
# Both tigers in this world are MUZZLED: three solid squares and one square of
# water. BoardShoot accepts a target square that is `Walkable or E_WATER`
# (GAME.PAS:1246) but ElementLionTick — which ElementTigerTick ends by calling —
# moves only onto a Walkable one, so a tiger with a water muzzle fires forever
# and never takes a step. That is what makes a tiger comparable at all: its
# firing half is pure Signum arithmetic off the player's position, while its
# moving half is CalcDirectionSeek, which is only draw-free when creature and
# player share a row or a column (see beast.scn). P2 27 forces the firing gate
# `(Random(10) * 3) <= (P2 mod $80)`, whose draw tops out at 27; P2 155 is the
# same 27 with bit 7 set, which is what makes the second tiger fire STARS.
#
# Fire Bay, row 13 — the bullet tiger at 30,13, shooting west down the arrival
# row. Its stream is the clock the whole board runs on: a bullet every second
# frame, each travelling one square per frame, dying on the board edge west of
# the player. The player is only ever IN that stream while standing in row 13;
# the tiger keeps firing while the player is within two rows of it, but the
# bullets always travel row 13, so stepping off the row is enough. Stations:
#   - two ammo squares at 2,13 and 3,13 (+5 each, with the one-time hint)
#   - the player shoots east into the oncoming stream, which pins BOTH sides of
#     ElementBulletTick's ownership test at once. A player bullet may damage
#     anything Destructible, so it attacks the enemy bullet it meets and both
#     die with two DamageStat clicks; an enemy bullet may damage only the
#     player, so when the enemy bullet is the one that ticks into the square it
#     simply removes itself, silently. Which happens on a given frame is decided
#     by stat order, so the player's bullet walks east through the stream eating
#     roughly one bullet per frame before a collision finally goes the other way.
#   - an enemy bullet reaches the player: 100 health -> 90. The mirror of that
#     branch — a PLAYER bullet damaging a player — is the friendly-fire
#     deviation and is deliberately not exercised here.
#
# Fire Bay, row 8 — what a player bullet does at range, and the two ricochet
# branches that are not the head-on one ORCLSHOT already pinned:
#   - a bear at 12,8 (P1 8: it moves only along the player's own row) charges
#     west and is shot dead at range. Score 0 -> 1 is ElementBulletTick's
#     ScoreValue credit, read off the sidebar.
#   - the second shot runs the length of the row, over the water at 16,8
#     (bullets fly over water, ELEMENTS.PAS ElementBulletTick), and is stopped
#     by the solid at 19,8. The ricochet at 18,9 is BELOW the bullet's own
#     square, which is the `Board.Tiles[X + StepY][Y + StepX]` branch: it turns
#     the bullet NORTH, away from the ricochet, and it destroys the breakable
#     at 18,5 four squares up.
# Fire Bay, row 16 — the mirror: the ricochet at 16,15 is ABOVE the bullet, the
#   `Board.Tiles[X - StepY][Y - StepX]` branch, and the bullet turns SOUTH into
#   the breakable at 16,19. Taking both proves the two branches are not
#   interchangeable.
#
# Star Bay (reached over the west edge) — the star tiger at 50,13 firing east
# at a player standing in its own row, so ElementStarTick's CalcDirectionSeek is
# forced onto the horizontal every time. A star is not a bullet: it lives 100
# ticks, moves only on even P2, cannot be shot (Destructible false) and attacks
# E_PLAYER and E_BREAKABLE alike. The breakable at 56,13 takes the first star;
# the ones behind it reach the player, 10 health each.
#
# What is NOT here, deliberately: a point-blank shot in either direction. The
# fork's BoardShoot inverts vanilla's `(Element = E_PLAYER) = Boolean(source)`
# ownership test, so a player cannot shoot an adjacent monster and an adjacent
# monster cannot shoot the player — the M16.5 finding, filed as gap task M16.5a
# and pinned by TestPointBlankShotOwnershipGap. Every tiger here is kept more
# than two columns from the player for the same reason.
world ORCLFIRE
seed 0
phase
boot 240
capture title
play
# Fire Hub: unpause and cross the east border opening at 60,13.
move right
move right
move right
move right
move right
capture arrive
# Two ammo squares, then a shot east into the oncoming stream.
move right
move right
shoot right
capture shot-out
settle 4
capture bullets-meet
settle 14
capture bullets-eaten
settle 30
capture player-hit
# Out of row 13 and up the western corridor into the bear's row.
move up
move up
move up
move up
move up
capture in-lane
shoot right
settle 12
capture bear-shot
shoot right
settle 30
capture ricochet-north
# Down to row 16 for the mirror-image ricochet.
move down
move down
move down
move down
move down
move down
move down
move down
shoot right
settle 30
capture ricochet-south
# Back up to the arrival row and out over the west edge into Star Bay.
move up
move up
move up
move left
move left
move left
capture arrive-star
settle 12
capture star-breakable
settle 20
capture star-hit
settle 4
capture star-hit-again
